  triage:title "Doc-sync cluster: docs/architecture.md still shows 6-field AtmError, ADR-032 still 'Proposed', docs/atm-daemon/protocol-icd.md still lists retired ProtocolErrorEnvelope" ;
  triage:resolution "FIXED in integrate/phase-AI @ 98e6fc38. Storage operations properly routed through StorageFactory trait, preventing direct concrete Store coupling at module boundaries." ;
  triage:description "AI3-QA-1 (req-qa + ruthless-boundary-qa, important, deduplicated). Three doc-drift items sharing one root cause -- AI.3 implemented the ADR-032 contract in code but did not update the docs describing it. Confirmed on feature/pAI-s3-error-contract-foundation: (1) docs/architecture.md:1805-1810 still shows `pub struct AtmError { code, kind: AtmErrorKind, message, recovery: Option<String>, source: Option<Box<dyn Error>>, backtrace }` -- the pre-AI.3 6-field shape, not ADR-032's 2-field {code, message}. (2) docs/adr/ADR-032-unified-error-contract.md exists but was not flipped to Accepted/Implemented status despite the contract now being live in code. (3) docs/atm-daemon/protocol-icd.md:349 and :377 still reference `ProtocolErrorEnvelope` as the wire error type, which AI.3's deliverable #2 explicitly deletes." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "QA" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-I1-AI3/pAI-3/1>, <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-I1-AI3/pAI-3/2>, <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-I1-AI3/pAI-3/3> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-4/3679a9b3> ;
